Z||000009||Shaun41178||04-22-2001||04:28 PM||||I don't know if Mach 10 was joking or not but if he wasn't then I am a little dissapointed in his attitude.<P>Sorry but some people are concerned about getting more performance out of our V6 Fiero's.  Most people on here are just talk.  You know what I hate talkers and not doers.  Plus people on here are so d@amn cheap when it comes to getting more hp from your Fiero.  God you spend $2k on a car and expect it to perform like a vette for $15.  <P>I can't believe that many of you complain how an intake for a Fiero that has not been made for 13 years costs $175.  Get a clue people.  Pick up a mag and see how much performance products cost for an import.  Then you complain that there are not enough FIero vendors.  THe fiero is such a small part of the market which is why noone makes performance parts for it besides the fact it isn't made anymore.  Plus the fact that the 2.8 engine is a piece of crap to try and ring power out of in comparison to todays modern cars.  Even the 3.4<P>Oh oh $3k for a Turbo kit?  Stop whining and look at the rest of the market for a turbo kit.  C5 kit costs what $5k?  Import kits cost $3k.  BE happy it is only $3k and that someone spent the time and research to even make one for such a limited market in the first place.  Oh $3k is too much I will make my own.  Hey guess what no you won't cause you would rather complain about how someone charges $3k for a kit.  Be lucky its not $5k cause it is such a limited market and demand is low.  Yea there are some on here that have spent a decent amount of money on their Fiero to make it faster.  However the majority do not and just talk and complain.<P>Also remember that most people that supply Fiero performance parts are doing it as a hobby and not to get rich cause you can't get rich off of these cars.  So when someone says they are going to supply some new part to get more power and it is not done when they say it might be done then don't give them h*ll for it.  Its a hobby not a million dollar business with molds that just pump this stuff out.<P>Cut them some slack.  I have been waiting for like a year now to see this setup and buy one and dyno test it.  Am I upset about it?  No cause I would rather have them have it done and done right then to ship off some product that is half @ss just to get it out faster to keep you people happy when you aren't even going to spend the money on it anyway.  <P>Better yet just build your own and see how long it takes you.  Thats what I thought.<P>Hey Eric keep my email on file Shaun41178@aol.com and let me know when it is done.  Or just send Travis an email and I am sure he will let me know about it. THanks||||reg||1
Z||000010||Nashco||04-22-2001||06:16 PM||||Well, it seems like you got the wrong impression.  I wasn't ridiculing the project, just humored in the situation.  I am not against somebody developing parts for our cars, and I am not above paying the price for something.  <P>I'll be honest and admit I won't pay a lot of money for stuff, but that's because I'm without the resources (college student) right now.  I am studying to be an automotive engineer, and I have all the ambition in the world, just not the cash to support it right now.  I am currently trying to learn how to program e-proms, because I think that the aftermarket ones are too pricey to get custom made if you are constantly doing mods.  I will never be done playing with my cars, so I think it will be most advantageous to learn how to program the e-proms before I get into replacing parts.  <P>I am one of those guys who is considering making parts for such a "limited market" because I'm tired of there being so much stuff available for other cars, but only for us at a high price (in most situations).  I also would like to clarify that there are many of us working on projects, but we don't advertise it until we have it installed and tested in our own cars.  Some people do, some don't....usually a great "unveiling" is at a car show or meet where you can show a finished product.  Just like in Detroit, some of us show finished vehicles, some show prototypes.<P>I'm all for developing some new stuff.  I find more fun in developing things than selling it to other people.  I was just humoring the situation up a little bit.  We all know the ol' "who's on first" comedy routine...it was frustrating as hell to them...but to the rest of us it was quite humorous.  Please don't feel offended, nothing was meant by it.<P>Good luck with your project!  I have been monitoring the site for updates, and I'm interested to see what you come up with.  I have some ideas as to how you're doing it, but I'm not going to make an ass out of myself and even try to guess <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000011||loafer87gt||04-22-2001||06:29 PM||||Just curious as to what all you guys have planned. Are you fabricating a new intake plenum as well as the dual throttle body setup? Anychance of fabricating an intake that would work with the the newer aluminum heads? Looking forward to it.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Mach10||04-22-2001||06:54 PM||||Looks like I was misunderstood also. That post had nothing to do with this thread, other than the "it's a secret" thing. <BR>*YES* It was a joke. Humor.<P>It was a slightly butchered (massacred) quote out of "Interesting Times" by Terry Pratchett, (the albatross scene. The one definitely NOT carrying a secret message. At least that's what reminded me of this) but I am sure I heard something like this on a radio comic show.<BR>It was not meant as anything except stab at human nature. The quote was partiallly directed (misdirected?) at Nashco, as the situation reminded me of that book (Cannot really think of how, but anyway) and partially to your statement of this being an "Area51" project, and wanting to keep it under wraps. I'm sorry if I found that statement rather amusing. *I* thought that you'd done it on purpose.<P>CMWest: I'm amazed at your uncanny ability of finding ANYTHING offensive about that post, but if there is a percieved slight, I do apologize for it. It was not meant as a stab at your work, hobby, whatever.<P>Shaun41178: That post did not have ANYTHING to do with Fieros, or Performance. You are putting words in my mouth. I am all for performance upgrades in ANY car. I just thought that calling a project "Area51" and under wraps while telling us almost everything we needed to know was hilarious. Again, I thought that CMWest had done it on purpose...<P>BTW: Dual TB for the 2.8 would kick ass. Count on me keeping an eye on that one.||||reg||11
