Z||000025||WKDFIRO||04-23-2001||01:39 PM||||I think that one only has to look at what has already come out of the shop of West Coast Fieros. The pictures that have been posted on this very forum should be proof positive that they put out PRODUCT. Sure people had been talking about 3.4 DOHC and 3800s, but it would seem that the proof is in the pudding. <P>Shaun I agree with you 110%. I too am getting tired of people crying about performance like the cost of headers. Buy three headers for an import and see how much it costs. Apples and oranges here! Import exhaust headers are one part BECAUSE ITS A FOUR CYLINDER THAT MEANS ONE VALVE HEAD! V6 HAVE 2 VALVE HEADS. Means you have to get TWO headers and usually the crossover pipe!<P>Most of us on this thread already know to kick back and let research and development take its course. The Twin Throttle Body from Fiero Area 51 (Sounds like a good name for West Coast Fieros performance aftermarket department!) will eventually see the light of day... though I know that I was tempted sneak a peak at FA51 when I was over there!<P>Watch out for mysterious vans in front of the shop guys! (Start the Mission Impossible music...)||||reg||6
