Z||000035||Slick781||04-23-2001||10:49 PM||||Is there something wrong with wanting to get maximum power and performance for minimal price??  I mean c'mon, theres alot of penny pinchers out there, but to say that is to put down the people who actually CANT afford really expensive stuff, but love cars- especially fieros.  Take me for example, i post constantly with questions about stuff, and always ask for price comparisons and cheap ways to do it. But heres my situation:<P>Im a 17 year old senior, who didnt buy the fiero, and didnt care for them at all untill sometime last year.  My sister originally bought it in like '96 and sold it to my brother after she was done with it.  It was crap as far as reliability.  Then my brother went in the navy andd left the car here, and it sat in the yard for a couple years.  He then gave it to my dad to repay a debt.  Still didnt the anything about the car.  Then my dad began to like it alot, and after quite a few months of him buying parts and being addicvted to this forum, i also caught the bug.  We've bought quitye a few parts, which we constantly have to keep secret from my mom  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> and we've done alot of work on it.  I love fieros now, and we just paid 300 bucks for an 85 gt that need ALOT of parts, expensive ones too.  And me, being a car lover always wants to modify the car somehow, more power, sweeter looks, etc... but we dont have that kind of money.  If i were to even ask my dad to buy something like $500 headers, he would laugh in my face <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  so i get on here and try to find cheap alternatives... VERY cheap.  And with me living in florida, and planning to attent a college in Massachusetts that is 33K per year, with only 25K being paid by financial aid, i really dont even mention anything to my dad as far as buying stuff goes.<P>I wish i could just bust open my bank account that contains a bit of money from a lawn care job i had... and splurge one day and load up on fiero stuff, but i cant... every bit of that money will go to college and college related stuff.<P>I wish i could just be a normal teenager who can afford to spend my work money on sweet stuff for the car (which isnt even MINE, either of them) or maybe even clothes sometimes, but i cant.  <P>Between me and my dad, we can build and do almost anything, the only problem we have is money.  Im not saying we're poor, but as far as spreading out our money, the fieros on on the bottom of the family priority list.<P>This wasnt meant to be like a POed reply or anything, yano... its just that today in Psychology we were talking about what makes us unhappy in our lives, and really there is very little in my life that makes me unhappy, because im not the type of person to let it.  But my answer was baseball, because so many things happen in it that i have no control over, but i love the game so much.... and then another chick said "lack of money", and i connected with that one too, and it got me thinkin bout it...<P>i guess it just kinda hit a rough spot when i read this, sorry for the rant.<P>David<P>||||reg||1
Z||000036||WKDFIRO||04-24-2001||03:47 AM||||Wow, that picture does suck...can't make heads or tails out of any of it....is it just sticking down into the middle of the plenum?<P>Fuel management is going to be the real trick of a twin TB set up. What good is getting a lot of hp if your gas mileage dives down to 10 mpg. Especially now a days! <BR>     On top of agressive fuel management, a progressive linkage might be a solution to fuel management as well as drivability. <P>Josh, I don't know if the setup could even be considered TPI. I only saw a picture of it at FOCOA Hq. Gloria had told me a little about it from the nationals I think but that was years ago. It was a very impressive setup with an injector for each cylinder. Must have had something for fuel management there! The best I can tell you is to contact Gloria at FOCOA. Tell them Anthony from Fieros West mentioned it to you. I would hope that the best they could do is give you a contact. I don't even know if it still exists.||||reg||10
Z||000037||saleenfiero||04-24-2001||02:15 PM||||Can someone please tell me the point of putting a dual TB on a stock 2.8?  Would that not only be feasible if the engine wasn't getting enough gas?<P>------------------<BR>'86 SE - My car is actually a MacLaren F1 with a Fiero body kit; or not.||||reg||6
Z||000038||Black88GT||04-24-2001||02:25 PM||||I don't think fuel management would be too big of an issue.  With an AFPR and a fuel gauge, you should be able to tune it properly.  This sounds like a cool idea actually the more I think about it.  Throw the battery in the front compartment and try to make an intake for that side.  Not sure how you could open up the pass. side qtr. panel for the air though.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000039||WKDFIRO||04-24-2001||02:59 PM||||On a stock 2.8, I think there might be some power gains but I think this set up would be more aimed at the tricked out 3.4s. <P>The main hurdle is to match the increaced amount of air with a proportional amount of fuel.<P>As for the passenger side intake, you would have to take out the battery tray. That was done for the Zumalt V8 conversion at Fiero Motorsports...loved that Fiero... ||||reg||6
Z||000040||85Josh||04-24-2001||04:58 PM||||WKD, I'll e-mail FOCOA later today, thanks! Meanwhile, I'll stop cluttering up this thread, and ask if anyone else has seen it.<P>------------------<BR>85 2M4(Lil' Bit)||||reg||14
Z||000041||BBBAD GT||04-24-2001||09:33 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Black88GT:<BR><B>On my friends 84 Corvette he has "dual" TB's</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Not dogging ya, but that cross-fire injection on 84 Vetts is at best laughable.<P>Also, an AFPR isn't the best method to tune a motor with more air through out its total operating range.  I bet you don't need that extra fuel pressure cruising down the highway at 2500 rpms, but you might at WOT if you have really opened up the motor.  <P>Just my experiences.<P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero/V8sig.jpg">        <P><A HREF="http://home.att.net/~nomercy5.0/V8Specs.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD V8 For Sale</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||1
